      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the advice on the dosage, i'll keep it at that level so i don't overdo it. i'm just trying to be really proactive about managing this.\n\nthe thing is, even though we're focusing on the stress side, the weakness in my arm and the word-finding thing are making me a little nervous. sometimes when that happens, i also get this really sharp, sudden pressure in my chest for a few seconds, almost like a tight band around me, and then it just goes away. \n\nsince these \"glitches\" are so brief and disappear almost immediately, it's probably just my body reacting to the extreme fatigue and stress, right? like, if it were something actually dangerous like a heart issue or a stroke, wouldn't it be more constant and not just go away in a minute? i'm really trying to avoid the whole hospital ordeal because i just can't deal with the stress or the bills right now, so i just need to be sure that these little episodes are just part of the burnout \"resetting\" process. you're pretty sure it's just the exhaustion then?",
